[b]WitcherFG 0.1.0-preview.1 — unpublished preview[/b]

WitcherFG attempts guarded, temporary Streamline import routing for The Witcher 3 Xbox PC package 5.0.4.0. No stable release or public download is available. [url=https://github.com/JrSneed28/WitcherFG/issues]Public support[/url] is available; vulnerabilities use private security reporting (../SECURITY.md). Player packaging and exact-candidate gameplay/install/upgrade/uninstall acceptance are Pending.

The earlier RTX 5070 Ti / driver 617.42 / Windows 26200 / 1440p diagnostic probe restored FG/MFG with manual ray tracing recovery. That probe does not verify the native launcher or a player ZIP. Native synthetic lifecycle fixtures are separately documented. Applied and RoutingAlreadyPresent confirm routing only; FPS ratios do not prove generated frames.

For a developer-built executable, close the game, keep the utility outside the game directory on a fixed local drive, and run WitcherFG.exe. Preserve existing game/mod DLLs and backups. No chainloading or manager coexistence is verified. The compiled build guard refuses unknown builds and late startup.

Error logging is the default; automatic runtime observation is Off. The SDK diagnostic catalog is empty, so unavailable activity fields remain Unknown. Explicit WitcherFG.exe --collect-support creates a local sanitized archive without uploads. Normal returned exits 0/2/3/4 differ from forced watchdog 1460/fallback 124 and immediate unsafe helper 3; forced helper death does not prove target exit or detach.

This is the shared player-facing source for channel summaries. Compatibility (compatibility.md), installation (installation.md), uninstall (uninstall.md), diagnostics (diagnostics.md), changelog (../CHANGELOG.md) and the canonical troubleshooting table (troubleshooting.md) supply detailed claims. The BBCode draft (NEXUS_DESCRIPTION.bbcode) is generated from these sources and remains unpublished. Packaging produces a candidate; actual gameplay/player acceptance remains Pending.

[b]Compatibility and evidence scope[/b]

Component | Evidence status | Native release status | Details
Xbox PC executable, menu 5.01 / package 5.0.4.0 | Verified: diagnostic probe | Pending | Measured fingerprints and temporary four-import redirection.
NVIDIA RTX 5070 Ti | Verified: diagnostic probe | Pending | Local Dynamic FG probe; visible world and smoother motion confirmed after manual RT reset.
NVIDIA driver 617.42 | Verified: diagnostic probe | Pending | Local probe used the original NVIDIA profile.
Windows 11 Pro build 26200, 2560 × 1440 | Verified: diagnostic probe | Pending | Measured local environment; other resolutions/window modes are untested.
Native WitcherFG launcher or installer ZIP | Pending | Pending | Native code and synthetic lifecycle tests exist; packaged game/player acceptance remains Pending.
Other NVIDIA GPUs | Untested | Pending | No extrapolation from the RTX 5070 Ti probe.
AMD GPUs | Untested | Pending | No support claim; no AMD FG backend is supplied.
Intel GPUs | Untested | Pending | No support claim; no Intel FG backend is supplied.
Steam executable | Untested | Pending | Initial compiled Xbox eligibility does not authorize this store/build.
Epic/GOG executables | Untested | Pending | Initial compiled Xbox eligibility does not authorize these stores/builds.
Other NVIDIA driver versions | Untested | Pending | Not independently verified.
Other upscaler/FG mods, Vortex, other mod managers | Untested | Pending | No named/versioned coexistence or manager test exists.
Black-screen resolution reported 2026-10-12 | Reported | Pending | User reports black screen resolved. Historical probes retained; cause and native gameplay FG remain unverified.
